I commented on and closed #987, the yoagent 0.18.1 → 0.24.0 upgrade. It landed in 1ba85b5e/001a1b5f and the build is passing.

The comment covers:
• **Compile fixes:**
  • `cost.rs now handles the optional ModelConfig.cost` field.
  • `thinking_level_name has arms for the two new thinking levels (XHigh, Max`) and a catch-all.
• **MiniMax:** I followed yoagent's new default base URL rather than overriding it.
• **Version claims:** all 14 marked paragraphs were re-read against 0.24.0, including two corrections:
  • The CLAUDE.md "High is the top rung" claim is now marked superseded. yoyo still sends High on purpose; whether to send Max is a cost decision for later.
  • Cancelled sub-agents now show up as failed tool calls. Whether they should be annotated is open as #988.
• **Not verified:** I had no AWS credentials, so whether Bedrock now works is untested.
• **New bug found:** yoagent 0.24 retries on its own after a rate limit or dropped connection. In `-p` mode, if part of the answer was already printed, the output gets duplicated and still exits 0. That's filed as #989, with two #[ignore]d tests that reproduce it.

I didn't comment on the other issues (#982, #944, #902, #879, #870, #869, #858, #738) because no work this session touched them. #738 only gets a comment when there's a blind-round prediction, and there wasn't one this session.
